Usage

    libzelda64 ships with a small suite of utilities, collectively called
    `libzelda64-utils`, which can be found under the `utils/` folder. They can
    be used to compress and decompress Nintendo 64 Zelda ROMs.

    To decompress a Nintendo 64 Zelda ROM:

        utils/decompress -M manifest.zmf compressed.z64 decompressed.z64

    The `-M` option creates a manifest of the ROM which is needed to recreate
    the same ROM with the compressor as decompression is destructive. To
    compress a decompressed ROM call:

        utils/compress -M manifest.zmf decompressed.z64 compressed.z64

    To make a compressed ROM in the same way Nintendo does, call:

        utils/compress --pad --fill ramp -M manifest.zmf in.z64 out.z64

    For more options, see `--help`.

Compiling

    Download the latest source tarball, and then:

        tar -xvf zelda64-x.y.z.tar.gz
        cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release      \
            -S ./zelda64-x.y.z                \
            -B /path/to/build-dir
        cmake --build /path/to/build-dir

    You will need CMake 3.21 or later, a C compiler that supports the C99
    standard, and libyaz0 version 0.1.
